      "content": "<h3 class=\"anat-section-title\">Speaking the Language: Directional Terms and Body Planes</h3><div class=\"anat-callout\">Precise anatomical language helps the veterinary team document findings clearly and communicate consistently.</div><div class=\"anat-tabs\" data-anat-tabs><div class=\"anat-tablist\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Directional terms\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" class=\"anat-tab is-active\" id=\"anat-tab-cranial\" data-anat-tab=\"cranial\" aria-controls=\"anat-panel-cranial\" aria-selected=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\">Cranial</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" class=\"anat-tab\" id=\"anat-tab-caudal\" data-anat-tab=\"caudal\" aria-controls=\"anat-panel-caudal\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">Caudal</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" class=\"anat-tab\" id=\"anat-tab-dorsal\" data-anat-tab=\"dorsal\" aria-controls=\"anat-panel-dorsal\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">Dorsal</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" class=\"anat-tab\" id=\"anat-tab-ventral\" data-anat-tab=\"ventral\" aria-controls=\"anat-panel-ventral\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">Ventral</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" class=\"anat-tab\" id=\"anat-tab-distal\" data-anat-tab=\"distal\" aria-controls=\"anat-panel-distal\" aria-selected=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\">Distal</button></div><div class=\"anat-tabpanels\"><div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"anat-tabpanel\" id=\"anat-panel-cranial\" data-anat-panel=\"cranial\" aria-labelledby=\"anat-tab-cranial\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"anat-direction-layout\"><div class=\"anat-direction-copy\"><h4>Cranial</h4><p>Toward the head.</p></div><img class=\"academy-image\" src=\"assets/media/anatomy-physiology/direction-cranial.jpg\" alt=\"Cranial directional term illustration\" width=\"1141\" height=\"766\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div></div><div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"anat-tabpanel\" id=\"anat-panel-caudal\" data-anat-panel=\"caudal\" aria-labelledby=\"anat-tab-caudal\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden><div class=\"anat-direction-layout\"><div class=\"anat-direction-copy\"><h4>Caudal</h4><p>Toward the tail.</p></div><img class=\"academy-image\" src=\"assets/media/anatomy-physiology/direction-caudal.jpg\" alt=\"Caudal directional term illustration\" width=\"1141\" height=\"766\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div></div><div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"anat-tabpanel\" id=\"anat-panel-dorsal\" data-anat-panel=\"dorsal\" aria-labelledby=\"anat-tab-dorsal\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden><div class=\"anat-direction-layout\"><div class=\"anat-direction-copy\"><h4>Dorsal</h4><p>Toward the back or upper surface.</p></div><img class=\"academy-image\" src=\"assets/media/anatomy-physiology/direction-dorsal.jpg\" alt=\"Dorsal directional term illustration\" width=\"1141\" height=\"766\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div></div><div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"anat-tabpanel\" id=\"anat-panel-ventral\" data-anat-panel=\"ventral\" aria-labelledby=\"anat-tab-ventral\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden><div class=\"anat-direction-layout\"><div class=\"anat-direction-copy\"><h4>Ventral</h4><p>Toward the belly or lower surface.</p></div><img class=\"academy-image\" src=\"assets/media/anatomy-physiology/direction-ventral.jpg\" alt=\"Ventral directional term illustration\" width=\"1141\" height=\"766\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div></div><div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"anat-tabpanel\" id=\"anat-panel-distal\" data-anat-panel=\"distal\" aria-labelledby=\"anat-tab-distal\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden><div class=\"anat-direction-layout\"><div class=\"anat-direction-copy\"><h4>Distal</h4><p>Farther from the body or point of attachment.</p></div><img class=\"academy-image\" src=\"assets/media/anatomy-physiology/direction-distal.jpg\" alt=\"Distal directional term illustration\" width=\"1141\" height=\"766\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></div></div></div></div><figure class=\"academy-figure anat-figure\"><img class=\"academy-image\" src=\"assets/media/anatomy-physiology/anatomical-terms.png\" alt=\"Anatomical directional terms: superficial, deep, and rostral\" width=\"1000\" height=\"630\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Superficial is near the surface, deep is toward the interior, and rostral is toward the nose.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"academy-figure anat-figure\"><img class=\"academy-image\" src=\"assets/media/anatomy-physiology/paw-surfaces.png\" alt=\"Palmar and plantar paw surface terms\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Palmar refers to the forepaw surface distal to the carpus; plantar refers to the hindpaw surface distal to the tarsus.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"anat-grid anat-grid--three\"><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Proximal</h4><p>Closer to the body or point of attachment.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Distal</h4><p>Farther from the body or point of attachment.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Medial</h4><p>Toward the median plane.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Lateral</h4><p>Away from the median plane.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Superficial</h4><p>Near the body surface.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Deep</h4><p>Toward the interior of the body.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Rostral</h4><p>Toward the nose.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Palmar</h4><p>Caudal surface of the forepaw distal to the carpus.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Plantar</h4><p>Caudal surface of the hindpaw distal to the tarsus.</p></div></div><h3 class=\"anat-section-title\">Body Planes in Animals</h3><div class=\"anat-section-head\"><p class=\"anat-eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 1</p><h3>Spin to Learn the Body Planes</h3><p>Start here. Spin the wheel to learn what each body plane means before completing the matching activity. A plane will not repeat until all four have been selected.</p></div><div class=\"anat-spinner\" data-anat-spinner data-anat-remaining-tpl=\"{n} plane{s} remaining\" data-anat-remaining-done=\"All planes reviewed\" data-anat-spin-label=\"Spin the Wheel\" data-anat-spin-done=\"All Planes Reviewed\"><div class=\"anat-spinner-layout\"><div class=\"anat-wheel-column\"><span class=\"anat-wheel-pointer\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><span class=\"anat-wheel\" data-anat-wheel aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"anat-wheel-label anat-wheel-label--median\">Median</span><span class=\"anat-wheel-label anat-wheel-label--sagittal\">Sagittal</span><span class=\"anat-wheel-label anat-wheel-label--transverse\">Transverse</span><span class=\"anat-wheel-label anat-wheel-label--dorsal\">Dorsal</span></span><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-btn anat-btn--primary\" data-anat-spin>Spin the Wheel</button><p class=\"anat-spinner-remaining\" data-anat-remaining role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">4 planes remaining</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-btn anat-btn--ghost\" data-anat-spin-reset>Reset Spinner</button></div><div class=\"anat-spinner-result\"><div class=\"anat-plane-result\" data-anat-plane-result=\"ready\"><span class=\"anat-result-kicker\">Ready</span><h4>Choose a Body Plane</h4><p>Spin the wheel to reveal a definition and a clinical application.</p></div><div class=\"anat-plane-result\" data-anat-plane-result=\"median\" data-anat-angle=\"0\" hidden><span class=\"anat-result-kicker\">Selected Plane</span><h4>Median Plane</h4><p><strong>Definition:</strong> Divides the body into equal right and left halves.</p><p><strong>Clinical connection:</strong> Useful when describing structures positioned directly on the midline.</p></div><div class=\"anat-plane-result\" data-anat-plane-result=\"sagittal\" data-anat-angle=\"90\" hidden><span class=\"anat-result-kicker\">Selected Plane</span><h4>Sagittal Plane</h4><p><strong>Definition:</strong> Runs parallel to the median plane and divides the body into unequal right and left portions.</p><p><strong>Clinical connection:</strong> Useful when describing structures located to one side of the midline.</p></div><div class=\"anat-plane-result\" data-anat-plane-result=\"transverse\" data-anat-angle=\"180\" hidden><span class=\"anat-result-kicker\">Selected Plane</span><h4>Transverse Plane</h4><p><strong>Definition:</strong> Divides the body into cranial and caudal portions.</p><p><strong>Clinical connection:</strong> Commonly represented in cross-sectional imaging such as CT scans.</p></div><div class=\"anat-plane-result\" data-anat-plane-result=\"dorsal\" data-anat-angle=\"270\" hidden><span class=\"anat-result-kicker\">Selected Plane</span><h4>Dorsal/Horizontal Plane</h4><p><strong>Definition:</strong> Divides the body into dorsal and ventral portions.</p><p><strong>Clinical connection:</strong> Useful when describing structures above or below a horizontal reference plane.</p></div></div></div></div><div class=\"anat-section-head\"><p class=\"anat-eyebrow\">ACTIVITY 2</p><h3>Match Each Description to the Correct Body Plane</h3><p>Now apply what you learned. Drag each description card into the correct category. On a phone or tablet, tap a card and then tap the matching category.</p></div><div class=\"anat-match\" data-anat-match><div class=\"anat-match-bank\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-anat-key=\"median\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Divides the body into equal right and left halves.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-anat-key=\"sagittal\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Runs parallel to the median plane and creates unequal right and left portions.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-anat-key=\"transverse\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Divides the body into cranial and caudal portions.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-card\" draggable=\"true\" data-anat-key=\"dorsal\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Divides the body into dorsal and ventral portions.</button></div><div class=\"anat-match-zones\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-zone\" data-anat-zone=\"median\"><strong>Median Plane</strong><span class=\"anat-match-slot\" data-anat-slot>Drop description here</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-zone\" data-anat-zone=\"sagittal\"><strong>Sagittal Plane</strong><span class=\"anat-match-slot\" data-anat-slot>Drop description here</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-zone\" data-anat-zone=\"transverse\"><strong>Transverse Plane</strong><span class=\"anat-match-slot\" data-anat-slot>Drop description here</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-match-zone\" data-anat-zone=\"dorsal\"><strong>Dorsal/Horizontal Plane</strong><span class=\"anat-match-slot\" data-anat-slot>Drop description here</span></button></div><div class=\"anat-activity-controls\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-btn anat-btn--primary\" data-anat-match-check>Check Answers</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"anat-btn anat-btn--ghost\" data-anat-match-reset>Reset Activity</button></div><p class=\"anat-feedback\" data-anat-match-feedback role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\" data-msg-incomplete=\"Place all four description cards before checking your answers.\" data-msg-all=\"Great work! All body-plane descriptions are in the correct categories.\" data-msg-partial=\"{n} of 4 are correct. Move the highlighted cards and try again.\"></p></div><details class=\"anat-support\"><summary>Body-plane quick reference</summary><div class=\"anat-grid anat-grid--two\"><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Median Plane</h4><p>Equal right and left halves.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Sagittal Plane</h4><p>Unequal right and left portions.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Transverse Plane</h4><p>Cranial and caudal portions.</p></div><div class=\"anat-card\"><h4>Dorsal/Horizontal Plane</h4><p>Dorsal and ventral portions.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"anat-section-head\"><p class=\"anat-eyebrow\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</p><h3>Directional Terms Knowledge Check</h3><p>Apply veterinary directional terminology to identify body locations accurately.</p></div>",
      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "Which term describes a structure closer to the animal's back?",
          "opts": [
            "Ventral",
            "Dorsal",
            "Medial",
            "Proximal"
